const e="2011-english1",o=2011,t="英语一",a="2011年英语一",i=[{id:"sec-cloze",type:"cloze",title:"英语知识运用",directions:"Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)",articles:[{id:"cloze-1",title:"完形填空",type:"cloze",blocks:[{type:"paragraph",content:'Ancient Greek philosopher Aristotle viewed laughter as "a bodily exercise precious to health." But '},{type:"blank",blankId:1},{type:"paragraph",content:" some claims to the contrary, laughing probably has little influence on physical fitness. Laughter does "},{type:"blank",blankId:2},{type:"paragraph",content:" short-term changes in the function of the heart and its blood vessels, "},{type:"blank",blankId:3},{type:"paragraph",content:" heart rate and oxygen consumption. But because hard laughter is difficult to "},{type:"blank",blankId:4},{type:"paragraph",content:" , a good laugh is unlikely to have "},{type:"blank",blankId:5},{type:"paragraph",content:" benefits the way, say, walking or jogging does. "},{type:"blank",blankId:6},{type:"paragraph",content:" , instead of straining muscles to build them, as exercise does, laughter apparently accomplishes the "},{type:"blank",blankId:7},{type:"paragraph",content:" . Studies dating back to the 1930s indicate that laughter "},{type:"blank",blankId:8},{type:"paragraph",content:" muscles, decreasing muscle tone for up to 45 minutes after the laugh dies down. Such bodily reaction might conceivably help "},{type:"blank",blankId:9},{type:"paragraph",content:" the effects of psychological stress. Anyway, the act of laughing probably does produce other types of "},{type:"blank",blankId:10},{type:"paragraph",content:" feedback that improve an individual's emotional state. "},{type:"blank",blankId:11},{type:"paragraph",content:" one classical theory of emotion, our feelings are partially rooted "},{type:"blank",blankId:12},{type:"paragraph",content:" physical reactions. It was argued at the end of the 19th century that humans do not cry "},{type:"blank",blankId:13},{type:"paragraph",content:" they are sad but they become sad when the tears begin to flow. Although sadness also "},{type:"blank",blankId:14},{type:"paragraph",content:" tears, evidence suggests that emotions can flow "},{type:"blank",blankId:15},{type:"paragraph",content:" muscular responses. In an experiment published in 1988, social psychologist Fritz Strack of the University of Würzburg in Germany asked volunteers to "},{type:"blank",blankId:16},{type:"paragraph",content:" a pen either with their teeth – thereby creating an artificial smile – or with their lips, which would produce a(n) "},{type:"blank",blankId:17},{type:"paragraph",content:" expression. Those forced to exercise their smiling muscles "},{type:"blank",blankId:18},{type:"paragraph",content:" more enthusiastically to funny cartoons than did those whose mouths were contracted in a frown, "},{type:"blank",blankId:19},{type:"paragraph",content:" that expressions may influence emotions rather than just the other way around. "},{type:"blank",blankId:20},{type:"paragraph",content:" , the physical act of laughter could improve mood."}]}],questions:[{id:1,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"among",B:"except",C:"despite",D:"like"},answer:"C",analysis:'despite 【线索】But 与 to the contrary 双重让步信号 本句句首已有 But 表转折，宾语又是 some claims to the contrary（一些相反的说法）， 紧接着主句却给出否定结论 laughing probably has little influence on physical fitness。 【选项】A) among ✗ 并列含义与让步逻辑相悖 contrary claims 一员，逻辑反了。 B) except ✗ 排除关系无处落地 C) despite ✓ 让步介词正面对接转折结论 despite 表"尽管"，把 some claims to the contrary 处理成让步成分，与主句 laughing probably has little influence on physical fitness 形成"尽管有反例，但作者仍坚持"的标准让步 结构，与句首 But 协同。 D) like ✗ 类比义不符合反向语境 【验证】代入后整句读作 "But despite some claims to the contrary, laughing probably has little influence on physical fitness"，正是先承认存在反向声音、再亮出作者结论，与',position:0},{id:2,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"reflect",B:"demand",C:"indicate",D:"produce"},answer:"D",analysis:'produce 【线索】does 强调 + 后文转折 But 助动词 Laughter does __(2)__ short-term changes 中 does 表强调"的确会"，紧接着 But because hard laughter is difficult to __(4)__, a good laugh is unlikely to have __(5)__ 【选项】A) reflect ✗ 因果方向反了 B) demand ✗ 把笑变成索取者 C) indicate ✗ 弱因果不及 produce 直接 D) produce ✓ 正向因果最契合 does 强调 produce 表"产生、引起"，与 does 的强调与下文 But 退让形成"短期确有产生 / 但无长期收 【验证】代入后 Laughter does __(2)__ short-term changes in the function of the heart and its blood vessels 读作 "Laughter does produce short-term changes"，与紧随的 But 让步',position:0},{id:3,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"stabilizing",B:"boosting",C:"impairing",D:"determining"},answer:"B",analysis:'boosting 【线索】hard laughter 暗示生理"升高" 本段提到 hard laughter is difficult to __(4)__ 与 walking or jogging 的类比——把笑与 【选项】A) stabilizing ✗ 稳定与"变化"矛盾 stabilizing"稳定"意味着不变动，正好与 changes"变化"自相矛盾。 B) boosting ✓ 上调心率与耗氧契合类运动反应 boosting 表"提升、增强"，把 heart rate and oxygen consumption 一起拉高，与"笑类似运 动"的暗示一致，是对 short-term changes 的合理具体化。 C) impairing ✗ 损伤色彩与全文基调相悖 D) determining ✗ "决定"无法解释具体短期变化 determining 表"决定、决定性影响"，过于抽象，对 heart rate 这种已经客观存在的指标谈不 【验证】代入后短语读作 "short-term changes in the function of the heart and its blood vessels, boosting heart rate and oxygen consumption"，等于给 changes 加上"上调心 率与耗氧"的具体说明，与下一句把笑类比为 walking or jogging 完全自洽。',position:0},{id:4,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"transmit",B:"sustain",C:"evaluate",D:"observe"},answer:"B",analysis:'sustain 【线索】因果链：因难以持久 → 长期收益不可能 本句 because hard laughter is difficult to __(4)__, a good laugh is unlikely to have __(5)__ benefits the way, say, walking or jogging does 用 because 给出因果：因为做不 【选项】A) transmit ✗ "传输"对象错位 B) sustain ✓ 维持义贴合"难以长时间持续" C) evaluate ✗ 评估义与因果链脱节 D) observe ✗ 观察义不连接收益结果 【验证】代入后整句读作 "because hard laughter is difficult to sustain, a good laugh is unlikely to have measurable benefits the way, say, walking or jogging does"，因果链清晰：难',position:0},{id:5,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"measurable",B:"manageable",C:"affordable",D:"renewable"},answer:"A",analysis:'measurable 【线索】上文 short-term changes 的可量化指标 上文已经用 heart rate and oxygen consumption 这种可量化指标说明"短期变化"，紧接 【选项】 A) measurable ✓ 可测量呼应上文心率耗氧指标 measurable"可测量的"承接上文 heart rate 与 oxygen consumption 的量化指标，把"运动型 B) manageable ✗ 可管理与上下文无对照 C) affordable ✗ 经济维度跑题 D) renewable ✗ 可再生用于能源等领域 【验证】代入后读作 "a good laugh is unlikely to have measurable benefits the way, say, walking or jogging does"，与上文用 heart rate、oxygen consumption 等量化指标讨',position:0},{id:6,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"In turn",B:"In fact",C:"In addition",D:"In brief"},answer:"B",analysis:'In fact 【线索】上段已破"健身"，本段进一步揭真相 上一段结论是 laughing probably has little influence on physical fitness——常识被否； 本段紧接着用 instead of straining muscles to build them, as exercise does, laughter apparently accomplishes the __(7)__ 揭示"笑不仅不练肌肉，反而做相反的事"。这是对上 【选项】A) In turn ✗ 序列承接非加深反差 B) In fact ✓ 事实上加深反常识结论 In fact 用来引出"事实上比刚才说的还更反常识"的论点，正好把 instead of straining C) In addition ✗ 并列追加无递进力度 D) In brief ✗ 总结口吻不符位置 【验证】代入后段首读作 "In fact, instead of straining muscles to build them, as exercise does, laughter apparently accomplishes the opposite"，与上一段"笑没有体能收益"形成"事实',position:0},{id:7,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"opposite",B:"impossible",C:"average",D:"expected"},answer:"A",analysis:'opposite 【线索】instead of 已锁定"相反"语义 本句 instead of straining muscles to build them, as exercise does, laughter apparently accomplishes the __(7)__ 里 instead of 已把"锻炼绷紧肌肉"否掉，紧接着空 【选项】 A) opposite ✓ 反义最贴 instead of opposite"相反的事"与 instead of 直接对接，加上下一段 laughter __(8)__ muscles, decreasing muscle tone 又证实笑会让肌肉放松而非收紧，构成完整反差链。 B) impossible ✗ 做不到与下句陈述事实矛盾 C) average ✗ 平均义与对照无关 D) expected ✗ "预期"与反差段意冲突 【验证】代入后读作 "instead of straining muscles to build them, as exercise does, laughter apparently accomplishes the opposite"，再配合下一句 laughter __(8)__ muscles, decreasing muscle tone 给出的"放松肌肉"实证，前后构成完整反差，符合 outline"提反',position:0},{id:8,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"hardens",B:"weakens",C:"tightens",D:"relaxes"},answer:"D",analysis:'relaxes 【线索】decreasing muscle tone 直接锁"放松" decreasing muscle tone for up to 45 minutes after the laugh dies down 已经写明"在 【选项】A) hardens ✗ 变硬与肌张力下降矛盾 hardens"使变硬"对应肌张力上升，与 decreasing muscle tone 方向相反。 B) weakens ✗ 削弱力气而非放松张力 C) tightens ✗ 绷紧与下降义反 tightens"使绷紧"与上空 opposite 以及 decreasing 都正面冲突。 D) relaxes ✓ 放松肌肉=肌张力下降 relaxes"使放松"正是 decreasing muscle tone 的同义改写，与上一空"做相反的事"一起把"笑放 【验证】代入后整句读作 "Studies dating back to the 1930s indicate that laughter relaxes muscles, decreasing muscle tone for up to 45 minutes after the laugh dies down"，',position:0},{id:9,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"aggravate",B:"generate",C:"moderate",D:"enhance"},answer:"C",analysis:`moderate 【线索】上文"放松肌肉"的正面铺垫 上一段刚说 laughter __(8)__ muscles, decreasing muscle tone 是放松效果，本段又用 might conceivably help 这种偏正面的措辞，且后面紧接 the act of laughing probably does produce other types of __(10)__ feedback that improve an individual's 【选项】A) aggravate ✗ 恶化与正面立场冲突 B) generate ✗ 产生而非缓解 C) moderate ✓ 缓和最契合正面立场 D) enhance ✗ 增强压力效应与立场冲突 【验证】代入后读作 "Such bodily reaction might conceivably help moderate the effects of psychological stress"，承接上段"笑放松肌肉"的生理铺垫，引出本段"笑能改善情绪"的主 旨，符合 outline"切换到情绪轴"的过渡。`,position:0},{id:10,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"physical",B:"mental",C:"subconscious",D:"internal"},answer:"A",analysis:`physical 【线索】上文已说"放松肌肉"是身体反馈 上一段 laughter __(8)__ muscles, decreasing muscle tone 已经是"身体上的反馈"，本句 other types of __ feedback 指的是"除身体之外的别的反馈"……但作者的逻辑是"act of laughing (身体动作)→产生别的身体反馈→改善情绪"。下一句 our feelings are partially rooted __(12)__ physical reactions 也说情绪根植于身体反应，说明此处所谈的 other 【选项】 A) physical ✓ 身体反馈契合下句情绪根植身体反应 physical"身体的"与下句 our feelings are partially rooted __(12)__ physical reactions 严丝合 缝，整段的论点就是"身体反应→情绪改变"，feedback 必须是 physical。 B) mental ✗ 情绪本身不算反馈源头 C) subconscious ✗ 潜意识无文本支撑 D) internal ✗ 范围模糊不及 physical 准确 internal"内部的"过于笼统，无法精准对接下句 physical reactions 的明确指向。 【验证】代入后读作 "the act of laughing probably does produce other types of physical feedback that improve an individual's emotional state"，与下一句 our feelings are partially rooted __(12)__ physical reactions 完美对接，作者"身体→情绪"的链条立得住。`,position:0},{id:11,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"Except for",B:"According to",C:"Due to",D:"As for"},answer:"B",analysis:'According to 【线索】主句是"一种经典理论"的观点复述 主句 our feelings are partially rooted __(12)__ physical reactions 正是 one classical theory of emotion 的观点内容；下文 It was argued at the end of the 19th century that humans do not cry __(13)__ they are sad but they become sad when the tears 【选项】A) Except for ✗ 排除义没有对照对象 B) According to ✓ 援引依据正对接观点复述 According to"根据"标准地把 one classical theory of emotion 当作援引来源，主句正是其观 C) Due to ✗ 原因义无因果 D) As for ✗ 话题切换义不符 【验证】代入后读作 "According to one classical theory of emotion, our feelings are partially rooted in physical reactions"，构成"根据某理论，观点是……"的标准句式，与下句历史溯',position:0},{id:12,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"with",B:"on",C:"in",D:"at"},answer:"C",analysis:'in 【线索】be rooted in 是固定搭配 本句 our feelings are partially rooted __(12)__ physical reactions 框架就是 be rooted 【选项】A) with ✗ with 不与 rooted 搭配 with 与 rooted 不构成固定搭配，含义不通。 B) on ✗ on 多搭 based 而非 rooted on 常见于 be based on，rooted on 不是英语固定搭配。 C) in ✓ be rooted in 即"根植于" in 与 rooted 构成固定搭配 be rooted in，表示"根植于、源自"，与"情绪根植于身体反应"完美 D) at ✗ at 与 rooted 搭配生硬 【验证】代入后读作 "our feelings are partially rooted in physical reactions"，与紧邻上空',position:0},{id:13,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"unless",B:"until",C:"if",D:"because"},answer:"D",analysis:'because 【线索】but 后给出真正因果方向 but 后给出 they become sad when the tears begin to flow，意思是"先哭，然后才感到 【选项】A) unless ✗ 条件义非因果 B) until ✗ 时间义无因果对照 C) if ✗ 条件假设过弱 D) because ✓ 因果义恰好被 but 反转 【验证】代入后整句读作 "humans do not cry because they are sad but they become sad when the tears begin to flow"——先否定常识因果"哭因悲"，再用 but 给出反向因果"先',position:0},{id:14,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"exhausts",B:"follows",C:"precedes",D:"suppresses"},answer:"C",analysis:'precedes 【线索】上段刚说"先流泪后悲伤" 上段 humans do not cry __(13)__ they are sad but they become sad when the tears begin to flow 已经主张"先哭后悲"，本句用 Although 让步、用 also 提示"sadness 也确 【选项】A) exhausts ✗ 耗尽眼泪偏离主题 B) follows ✗ 顺序反了 C) precedes ✓ 悲伤先于眼泪恰好对应让步 步、also 强调都吻合。 D) suppresses ✗ 压制义偏离论题 【验证】代入后整段开头读作 "Although sadness also precedes tears, evidence suggests that emotions can flow __(15)__ muscular responses"——先让步"承认常识方向"，再用',position:0},{id:15,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"into",B:"from",C:"towards",D:"beyond"},answer:"B",analysis:'from 【线索】下文实验：表情→情绪 下文 Those forced to exercise their smiling muscles __(18)__ more enthusiastically to funny cartoons than did those whose mouths were contracted in a frown 和总结 expressions may influence emotions rather than just the other way around 都说"表 即 from。 【选项】A) into ✗ 方向反，情绪流入肌肉 into 表"流入"，等于情绪流进肌肉反应，把因果颠倒，与下文结论 expressions may influence emotions 相反。 B) from ✓ 从肌肉反应中涌出契合下文结论 C) towards ✗ 朝向义无明确终点 D) beyond ✗ 超越义偏离话题 beyond"超越"在此完全说不通。 【验证】代入后读作 "emotions can flow from muscular responses"，与下文实验+结论一致：肌',position:0},{id:16,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"fetch",B:"bite",C:"pick",D:"hold"},answer:"D",analysis:'hold 【线索】either…or… 必须兼容两种姿势 either with their teeth – thereby creating an artificial smile – or with their lips, which would produce a(n) __(17)__ expression 描述两种用嘴姿势：用牙咬住笔→人造笑容；用 【选项】A) fetch ✗ 取来与实验姿势无关 B) bite ✗ 咬只对牙不对唇 bite"咬"对应用牙这一情形，但与 with their lips 不兼容，无法涵盖整个 either…or 结构。 C) pick ✗ 挑选义不符姿势 D) hold ✓ 中性动作兼容用牙与用唇 hold"含住、衔住"作为中性动词，既能用 with teeth 也能用 with lips，正好涵盖 either…or 两 【验证】代入后整句读作 "asked volunteers to hold a pen either with their teeth – thereby creating an artificial smile – or with their lips, which would produce a(n) __(17)__',position:0},{id:17,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"disappointed",B:"excited",C:"joyful",D:"indifferent"},answer:"A",analysis:'disappointed 【线索】下文 frown 直接锁定表情 下文 those whose mouths were contracted in a frown 已点明"嘴部紧缩成皱眉表情"， frown 是"皱眉/不悦"，与 smile 直接对立——故空格表达的就是"不悦/失望"。 【选项】 A) disappointed ✓ 失望表情与 frown 同义 disappointed"失望的"与下文 frown"皱眉"是同一种负面表情的不同表述，与 smile 形成清晰 B) excited ✗ 兴奋与皱眉相反 excited"兴奋的"是正向情绪，与 frown 矛盾。 C) joyful ✗ 高兴等同 smile 同向 joyful"喜悦的"是 smile 同义，没法与 artificial smile 形成对立。 D) indifferent ✗ 冷漠非皱眉 indifferent"漠然的"不是皱眉这种带情绪的表情，与下文 frown 不对应。 【验证】代入后整句读作 "with their lips, which would produce a(n) disappointed expression"，与下文 those whose mouths were contracted in a frown 形成同义改写：',position:0},{id:18,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"adapted",B:"catered",C:"turned",D:"reacted"},answer:"D",analysis:'reacted 【线索】more enthusiastically + funny cartoons 是刺激-反应 Those forced to exercise their smiling muscles __(18)__ more enthusiastically to funny cartoons than did those whose mouths were contracted in a frown 句意是"对 enthusiastically 这种程度副词修饰的也是"反应程度"，故框架是 react to。 【选项】A) adapted ✗ 适应环境而非反应刺激 adapted + to 表"适应环境"，funny cartoons 不是环境，是即时刺激。 B) catered ✗ 迎合需求与实验不符 C) turned ✗ 求助/转向方向不对 turned + to 表"求助、转向"，不是对动画的笑声反应。 D) reacted ✓ 对刺激源做出反应 reacted + to 表"对……做出反应"，与 funny cartoons 这一刺激源 + enthusiastically 的程度副 【验证】代入后读作 "Those forced to exercise their smiling muscles reacted more enthusiastically to funny cartoons than did those whose mouths were contracted in',position:0},{id:19,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"suggesting",B:"requiring",C:"mentioning",D:"supposing"},answer:"A",analysis:'suggesting 【线索】实验结果与可能性结论 前半段是实验结果"咬笔促笑组反应更热烈"，后半 that 从句是 expressions may influence emotions rather than just the other way around——一个含 may 的可能性结论。结果 【选项】 A) suggesting ✓ 暗示推论对接 may suggesting"暗示"与 that 从句 may influence 形成"研究结果暗示可能性"的标准学术句型，准 B) requiring ✗ 要求义不属推论范畴 C) mentioning ✗ 提及义太轻 D) supposing ✗ 假设义无证据感 【验证】代入后读作 "…, suggesting that expressions may influence emotions rather than just the other way around"，前是实验结果，后是含 may 的推论，正好用 suggesting 串',position:0},{id:20,articleId:"cloze-1",type:"cloze",question:"",options:{A:"Eventually",B:"Consequently",C:"Similarly",D:"Conversely"},answer:"C",analysis:`Similarly 【线索】上句"表情→情绪"与本句"笑→心情"是同构推广 上句结论 expressions may influence emotions rather than just the other way around 谈的是"表情影响情绪"，本句 the physical act of laughter could improve mood 把同 样地"。 【选项】A) Eventually ✗ 时间终点义无对应 B) Consequently ✗ 因果义过强 Consequently"因此、所以"暗示严格因果，但 the physical act of laughter 与上句 expressions C) Similarly ✓ 同样地把同构逻辑推广到笑 绪"，与 outline 主旨一致。 D) Conversely ✗ 反义副词与同向推广冲突 【验证】代入后读作 "Similarly, the physical act of laughter could improve mood"，把上句"表 OVERVIEW · 通读建境 出 laughing probably has little influence on physical fitness，真正有意义的不是体能收 益，而是 the act of laughing probably does produce other types of __(10)__ feedback that improve an individual's emotional state 所暗示的——身体动作（笑、做表情）可以反过来 第 1 段先破后立：先引亚里士多德观点，再用 But __(1)__ some claims to the contrary, laughing probably has little influence on physical fitness 转入反驳；第 2 段进一步揭示笑 与锻炼的反差：instead of straining muscles to build them, as exercise does, laughter apparently accomplishes the __(7)__；第 3 段把话题从体能切到情绪，引出经典情绪理论 our feelings are partially rooted __(12)__ physical reactions；第 4 段用 Strack 的咬笔实验 佐证 expressions may influence emotions rather than just the other way around，最后回 扣主旨 the physical act of laughter could improve mood。 SENTENCE INSIGHTS · 句子精讲 10 Ancient Greek philosopher Aristotle viewed laughter as "a bodily exercise precious to health." But despite some claims to the contrary, laughing probably has little influence on physical fitness. Laughter does produce short-term changes in the function of the heart and its bl...`,position:0}]},{id:"sec-reading",type:"reading",title:"阅读理解",directions:"Read the following four texts. Answer the questions after each text by choosing A, B, C or D. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. (40 points)",articles:[{id:"text-1",title:"Text 1",type:"reading",blocks:[{type:"paragraph",content:`The decision of the New York Philharmonic to hire Alan Gilbert as its next music director has been the talk of the classical-music world ever since the sudden announcement of his appointment in 2009. For the most part, the response has been favorable, to say the least. "Hooray! At last!" wrote Anthony Tommasini, a sober-sided classical-music critic. One of the reasons why the appointment came as such a surprise, however, is that Gilbert is comparatively little known. Even Tommasini, who had advocated Gilbert's appointment in the Times, calls him "an unpretentious musician with no air of the formidable conductor about him." As a description of the next music director of an orchestra that has hitherto been led by musicians like Gustav Mahler and Pierre Boulez, that seems likely to have struck at least some Times readers as faint praise. For my part, I have no idea whether Gilbert is a great conductor or even a good one. To be sure, he performs an impressive variety of interesting compositions, but it is not necessary for me to visit Avery Fisher Hall, or anywhere else, to hear interesting orchestral music. All I have to do is to go to my CD shelf, or boot up my computer and download still more recorded music from iTunes. Devoted concertgoers who reply that recordings are no substitute for live performance are missing the point. For the time, attention, and money of the art-loving public, classical instrumentalists must compete not only with opera houses, dance troupes, theater companies, and museums, but also with the recorded performances of the great classical musicians of the 20th century. These recordings are cheap, available everywhere, and very often much higher in artistic quality than today's live performances; moreover, they can be "consumed" at a time and place of the listener's choosing. The widespread availability of such recordings has thus brought about a crisis in the institution of the traditional classical concert. One possible response is for classical performers to program attractive new music that is not yet available on record. Gilbert's own interest in new music has been widely noted: Alex Ross, a classical-music critic, has described him as a man who is capable of turning the Philharmonic into "a markedly different, more vibrant organization." But what will be the nature of that difference? Merely expanding the orchestra's repertoire will not be enough. If Gilbert and the Philharmonic are to succeed, they must first change the relationship between America's oldest orchestra and the new audience it hopes to attract.`}]},{id:"text-2",title:"Text 2",type:"reading",blocks:[{type:"paragraph",content:`When Liam McGee departed as president of Bank of America in August, his explanation was surprisingly straight up. Rather than cloaking his exit in the usual vague excuses, he came right out and said he was leaving "to pursue my goal of running a company." Broadcasting his ambition was "very much my decision," McGee says. Within two weeks, he was talking for the first time with the board of Hartford Financial Services Group, which named him CEO and chairman on September 29. McGee says leaving without a position lined up gave him time to reflect on what kind of company he wanted to run. It also sent a clear message to the outside world about his aspirations. And McGee isn't alone. In recent weeks the No. 2 executives at Avon and American Express quit with the explanation that they were looking for a CEO post. As boards scrutinize succession plans in response to shareholder pressure, executives who don't get the nod also may wish to move on. A turbulent business environment also has senior managers cautious of letting vague pronouncements cloud their reputations. As the first signs of recovery begin to take hold, deputy chiefs may be more willing to make the jump without a net. In the third quarter, CEO turnover was down 23% from a year ago as nervous boards stuck with the leaders they had, according to Liberum Research. As the economy picks up, opportunities will abound for aspiring leaders. The decision to quit a senior position to look for a better one is unconventional. For years executives and headhunters have adhered to the rule that the most attractive CEO candidates are the ones who must be poached. Says Korn/Ferry senior partner Dennis Carey: "I can't think of a single search I've done where a board has not instructed me to look at sitting CEOs first." Those who jumped without a job haven't always landed in top positions quickly. Ellen Marram quit as chief of Tropicana a decade ago, saying she wanted to be a CEO. It was a year before she became head of a tiny Internet-based commodities exchange. Robert Willumstad left Citigroup in 2005 with ambitions to be a CEO. He finally took that post at a major financial institution three years later. Many recruiters say the old disgrace is fading for top performers. The financial crisis has made it more acceptable to be between jobs or to leave a bad one. "The traditional rule was it's safer to stay where you are, but that's been fundamentally inverted," says one headhunter. "The people who've been hurt the worst are those who've stayed too long."`}]},{id:"text-3",title:"Text 3",type:"reading",blocks:[{type:"paragraph",content:`The rough guide to marketing success used to be that you got what you paid for. No longer. While traditional "paid" media – such as television commercials and print advertisements – still play a major role, companies today can exploit many alternative forms of media. Consumers passionate about a product may create "earned" media by willingly promoting it to friends, and a company may leverage "owned" media by sending e- mail alerts about products and sales to customers registered with its Web site. The way consumers now approach the process of making purchase decisions means that marketing's impact stems from a broad range of factors beyond conventional paid media. Paid and owned media are controlled by marketers promoting their own products. For earned media, such marketers act as the initiator for users' responses. But in some cases, one marketer's owned media become another marketer's paid media – for instance, when an e-commerce retailer sells ad space on its Web site. We define such sold media as owned media whose traffic is so strong that other organizations place their content or e-commerce engines within that environment. This trend, which we believe is still in its infancy, effectively began with retailers and travel providers such as airlines and hotels and will no doubt go further. Johnson & Johnson, for example, has created BabyCenter, a stand-alone media property that promotes complementary and even competitive products. Besides generating income, the presence of other marketers makes the site seem objective, gives companies opportunities to learn valuable information about the appeal of other companies' marketing, and may help expand user traffic for all companies concerned. The same dramatic technological changes that have provided marketers with more (and more diverse) communications choices have also increased the risk that passionate consumers will voice their opinions in quicker, more visible, and much more damaging ways. Such hijacked media are the opposite of earned media: an asset or campaign becomes hostage to consumers, other stakeholders, or activists who make negative allegations about a brand or product. Members of social networks, for instance, are learning that they can hijack media to apply pressure on the businesses that originally created them. If that happens, passionate consumers would try to persuade others to boycott products, putting the reputation of the target company at risk. In such a case, the company's response may not be sufficiently quick or thoughtful, and the learning curve has been steep. Toyota Motor, for example, alleviated some of the damage from its recall crisis earlier this year with a relatively quick and well-orchestrated social-media response campaign, which included efforts to engage with consumers directly on sites such as Twitter and the social-news site Digg.`}]},{id:"text-4",title:"Text 4",type:"reading",blocks:[{type:"paragraph",content:`It's no surprise that Jennifer Senior's insightful, provocative magazine cover story, "I love My Children, I Hate My Life," is arousing much chatter – nothing gets people talking like the suggestion that child rearing is anything less than a completely fulfilling, life-enriching experience. Rather than concluding that children make parents either happy or miserable, Senior suggests we need to redefine happiness: instead of thinking of it as something that can be measured by moment-to-moment joy, we should consider being happy as a past-tense condition. Even though the day-to-day experience of raising kids can be soul-crushingly hard, Senior writes that "the very things that in the moment dampen our moods can later be sources of intense gratification and delight." The magazine cover showing an attractive mother holding a cute baby is hardly the only Madonna-and-child image on newsstands this week. There are also stories about newly adoptive – and newly single – mom Sandra Bullock, as well as the usual "Jennifer Aniston is pregnant" news. Practically every week features at least one celebrity mom, or mom-to-be, smiling on the newsstands. In a society that so persistently celebrates procreation, is it any wonder that admitting you regret having children is equivalent to admitting you support kitten-killing? It doesn't seem quite fair, then, to compare the regrets of parents to the regrets of the childless. Unhappy parents rarely are provoked to wonder if they shouldn't have had kids, but unhappy childless folks are bothered with the message that children are the single most important thing in the world: obviously their misery must be a direct result of the gaping baby-size holes in their lives. Of course, the image of parenthood that celebrity magazines like Us Weekly and People present is hugely unrealistic, especially when the parents are single mothers like Bullock. According to several studies concluding that parents are less happy than childless couples, single parents are the least happy of all. No shock there, considering how much work it is to raise a kid without a partner to lean on; yet to hear Sandra and Britney tell it, raising a kid on their "own" (read: with round-the-clock help) is a piece of cake. It's hard to imagine that many people are dumb enough to want children just because Reese and Angelina make it look so glamorous: most adults understand that a baby is not a haircut. But it's interesting to wonder if the images we see every week of stress-free, happiness-enhancing parenthood aren't in some small, subconscious way contributing to our own dissatisfactions with the actual experience, in the same way that a small part of us hoped getting "the Rachel" might make us look just a little bit like Jennifer Aniston.`}]}],questions:[{id:21,articleId:"text-1",type:"reading",question:"We learn from Paragraph 1 that Gilbert's appointment has____",options:{A:"incurred criticism.",B:"raised suspicion.",C:"received acclaim.",D:"aroused curiosity."},answer:"C",analysis:`【判型】We learn from Paragraph 1 that 这种 "我们从第 X 段得知" 的句式要求答案直接来自段内 【拆句】Gilbert's appointment has____ 主谓后接现在完成时空位,空位要填的是动词词组,所以四个 选项都是 V+宾语 的结构(如 received acclaim);理解上无陷阱。 【定位】P1 For the most part, the response has been favorable, to say the least. "Hooray! At last!" wrote Anthony Tommasini, a sober-sided classical-music critic. Tommasini 写道:"万岁!终于来了!" 【选项】A) 与原文相反 incurred criticism 意为 "招致批评",与原文 favorable 极性相反。 raised suspicion 表达 "引起怀疑",原文只字未提任何怀疑情绪,Tommasini 是 "叫好" 而 不是 "质疑"。 C) ✓ 正确 the response has been favorable, to say the least ↔ received acclaim Hooray! At last! ↔ received acclaim 预判 "正面评价" 与 received acclaim 在极性、范围上完全吻合,且 acclaim 不像 incurred criticism 那样反向,也不像 raised suspicion/aroused curiosity 那样偏离 aroused curiosity 表达 "引起好奇",原文虽然提到 Gilbert is comparatively little`,position:0},{id:22,articleId:"text-1",type:"reading",question:"Tommasini regards Gilbert as an artist who is____",options:{A:"influential.",B:"modest.",C:"respectable.",D:"talented."},answer:"B",analysis:`Tommasini认为Gilbert是一位____的艺术家 A) 有影响力 B) 谦逊 C) 值得尊敬 D) 有才华 【判型】Tommasini regards Gilbert as an artist who is____ 问的是 Tommasini 对 Gilbert 的客观 【拆句】主句 Tommasini regards Gilbert as an artist + 限制性定语从句 who is____,空位补的是表 【定位】P2 Even Tommasini, who had advocated Gilbert's appointment in the Times, calls him "an unpretentious musician with no air of the formidable conductor about him." 甚至 Tommasini——这位曾在《纽约时报》上力挺 Gilbert 任命的评论家——也只是把他 【选项】A) 无中生有 influential 强调有影响力,原文 Gilbert is comparatively little known 反而提示其知名 B) ✓ 正确 an unpretentious musician ↔ modest with no air of the formidable conductor about him ↔ modest (influential/respectable/talented) 都未在 Tommasini 的引语中出现对应表达。 respectable 意为 "令人尊敬的",但原文恰恰强调 "no air of the formidable talented 谈才华,Tommasini 的引语只评说 Gilbert 的 "气质姿态",没有评价其音乐`,position:0},{id:23,articleId:"text-1",type:"reading",question:"The author believes that the devoted concertgoers____",options:{A:"ignore the expenses of live performances.",B:"reject most kinds of recorded performances.",C:"exaggerate the variety of live performances.",D:"overestimate the value of live performances."},answer:"D",analysis:'【判型】The author believes that the devoted concertgoers____ 直接问作者对某群体的看法,答 【拆句】The author believes that the devoted concertgoers____ 是 believe + that 宾语从句结 【定位】P4 Devoted concertgoers who reply that recordings are no substitute for live performance are missing the point. 【选项】A) 无中生有 ignore the expenses of live performances 说乐迷忽视现场票价,原文虽提到 For the time, attention, and money,但谈的是公众资源被各种艺术形式争夺,不是乐迷忽视 reject most kinds of recorded performances 说乐迷 "拒绝大多数录音演出",原文只提 exaggerate the variety of live performances 说乐迷夸大了现场演出的多样性,但原文 D) ✓ 正确 Devoted concertgoers who reply that recordings are no substitute for live performance are missing the point. ↔ overestimate the value of live performances For the time, attention, and money of the art-loving public, classical instrumentalists must compete not only with opera houses, dance troupes, theater companies, and museums, but also with the recorded performances of the great classical musicians of the 20th century. ↔ overestimate the value of live performances 预判 "高估现场" 与 overestimate the value of live performances 在评判方向、对 象、程度上完全吻合,且 over- 前缀正好对应 missing the point 所暗示的 "过分"。',position:0},{id:24,articleId:"text-1",type:"reading",question:"According to the text, which of the following is true of recordings?",options:{A:"They are often inferior to live concerts in quality.",B:"They are easily accessible to the general public.",C:"They help improve the quality of music.",D:"They have only covered masterpieces."},answer:"B",analysis:`【判型】which of the following is true of recordings 是典型 "关于 X 下列哪项为真" 的细节核对 【拆句】According to the text, which of the following is true of recordings? 一个 wh-疑问句,主 干是 which…is true of recordings;无复杂修饰。 【定位】P4 These recordings are cheap, available everywhere, and very often much higher in artistic quality than today's live performances; moreover, they can be "consumed" at a time and place of the listener's choosing. 【选项】A) 与原文相反 They are often inferior to live concerts in quality 说录音质量常低于现场,但原文恰恰 说 very often much higher in artistic quality than today's live performances—— B) ✓ 正确 available everywhere ↔ easily accessible to the general public cheap ↔ easily accessible to the general public 在四个选项中,只有 easily accessible to the general public 完整落在原文列出的 cheap + available everywhere 这两个属性上,既未夸大也未跑题。 They help improve the quality of music 说录音 "帮助改善了音乐的质量",但原文只比 They have only covered masterpieces 说录音 "只覆盖了名曲",原文虽提到 the recorded performances of the great classical musicians of the 20th century,但说`,position:0},{id:25,articleId:"text-1",type:"reading",question:"Regarding Gilbert's role in revitalizing the Philharmonic, the author feels____",options:{A:"doubtful.",B:"enthusiastic.",C:"confident.",D:"puzzled."},answer:"A",analysis:`A) 怀疑 B) 热情 C) 有信心 D) 困惑 【判型】the author feels____ 空位填 doubtful/enthusiastic/confident/puzzled 等情感形容词,本 【拆句】Regarding Gilbert's role in revitalizing the Philharmonic, the author feels____ 介词短 语 Regarding… 作状语限定话题范围,主句是 the author feels + 形容词;无陷阱,但要注意状 【选项】A) ✓ 正确 Merely expanding the orchestra's repertoire will not be enough. ↔ doubtful If Gilbert and the Philharmonic are to succeed, they must first change the relationship between America's oldest orchestra and the new audience it hopes to attract. ↔ doubtful enthusiastic 表达 "热情洋溢",但作者在末段连用 not be enough 与 must first change confident 表达 "有信心",原文中作者的两道 not enough/must first change 完全没给 SENTENCE INSIGHTS · 句子精讲 11 The decision of the New York Philharmonic to hire Alan Gilbert as its next music director has been the talk of the classical-music world ever since the sudden announcement of his appointment in 2009. One of the reasons why the appointment came as such a surprise, however, is that Gilbert is comparatively little known. For my part, I have no idea whether Gilbert is a great conductor or even a good one. To be sure, he performs an impressive variety of interesting compositions, but it is not necessary for me to visit Avery Fisher Hall, or anywhere else, to hear interesting orchestral music. All I have to do is to go to my CD shelf, or boot up my computer and download still more recorded music from iTunes. "All I have to do is ..." 是四六级和考研阅读中的常见句式,用主语从句表达 "我需要做的全部就是...", 后接并列表语,结构典型,掌握后可迁移到类似的 "What I need is ..." 或 "The o...`,position:0},{id:26,articleId:"text-2",type:"reading",question:"When McGee announced his departure, his manner can best be described as being____",options:{A:"arrogant.",B:"frank.",C:"self-centered.",D:"impulsive."},answer:"B",analysis:'【判型】his manner can best be described as being 问的是某一具体时刻 McGee 的表达方式， 【拆句】Q26 主干是 his manner can best be described as being ____，前面 When McGee announced his departure 是时间状语从句限定时间范围；考生只要把题干理解为「当 【定位】P1 Rather than cloaking his exit in the usual vague excuses, he came right out and said he was leaving "to pursue my goal of running a company." 【选项】A) 无中生有 arrogant 意为「傲慢、自负」，原文只说 McGee 直接说出自己想做 CEO 的目标 to pursue my goal of running a company，没有任何贬义评价；说出真实动机不等于 B) ✓ 正确 came right out and said ↔ frank Rather than cloaking his exit in the usual vague excuses ↔ frank self-centered 意为「以自我为中心」，原文 Broadcasting his ambition was "very much my decision," McGee says 是在说「公开抱负是我自己的决定」，强调的是决定 impulsive 意为「冲动的、未经深思的」，原文 came right out and said 强调「不绕 弯子」而非「未经深思」；下一段 McGee 还说 leaving without a position lined up gave him time to reflect on what kind of company he wanted to run，说明他离职',position:0},{id:27,articleId:"text-2",type:"reading",question:"According to Paragraph 2, senior executives' quitting may be spurred by____",options:{A:"their expectation of better financial status.",B:"their need to reflect on their private life.",C:"their strained relations with the boards.",D:"their pursuit of new career goals."},answer:"D",analysis:"【判型】题干 senior executives' quitting may be spurred by 在第二段内寻找一个明确给出的离职 【拆句】Q27 主干是 senior executives' quitting may be spurred by ____；情态动词 may 表示 【定位】P2 In recent weeks the No. 2 executives at Avon and American Express quit with the explanation that they were looking for a CEO post. 【选项】A) 无中生有 their expectation of better financial status 把动因归为「期待更好的财务状况」，但 their need to reflect on their private life 把原文 reflect on what kind of company 生活」（生活层面）——原文 reflect 的宾语是 company，不是 private life。 their strained relations with the boards 把原文 As boards scrutinize succession plans in response to shareholder pressure, executives who don't get the nod also D) ✓ 正确 they were looking for a CEO post ↔ their pursuit of new career goals the explanation that they were looking for a CEO post ↔ their pursuit of new career goals 预判「想去做 CEO」对应选项 their pursuit of new career goals，「CEO 职位」即 「新职业目标」的具体化；且段首 McGee 同例、段中 Avon/American Express 同",position:0},{id:28,articleId:"text-2",type:"reading",question:'The word "poached" (Line 3, Paragraph 4) most probably means____',options:{A:"approved of.",B:"attended to.",C:"hunted for.",D:"guarded against."},answer:"C",analysis:'A) 赞同 B) 处理 C) 猎取 D) 防范 【判型】题干 most probably means 是词义题的固定提问句式，问的是 poached 在上下文中的 【拆句】Q28 主干是 The word "poached" ... most probably means ____；其中 Line 3, 【定位】P4 For years executives and headhunters have adhered to the rule that the most attractive CEO candidates are the ones who must be poached. 【选项】A) 偷换概念 C) ✓ 正确 the most attractive CEO candidates are the ones who must be poached ↔ hunted for headhunters ↔ hunted for headhunters 反复出现暗示 hunt 词根，锁定 C。 guarded against 意为「被提防、被防范」，方向与原文相反——原文是「最有吸引力',position:0},{id:29,articleId:"text-2",type:"reading",question:"It can be inferred from the last paragraph that____",options:{A:"top performers used to cling to their posts.",B:"loyalty of top performers is getting out-dated.",C:"top performers care more about reputations.",D:"it's safer to stick to the traditional rules."},answer:"A",analysis:`【判型】It can be inferred from the last paragraph 同时具备推断信号词和明示段号，是典型的 【拆句】Q29 是 It can be inferred from the last paragraph that ____ 的形式主语句，主语 It 形 【定位】P6 "The traditional rule was it's safer to stay where you are, but that's been fundamentally inverted," says one headhunter. "The people who've been hurt the worst are those who've stayed too long." 【选项】A) ✓ 正确 The traditional rule was it's safer to stay where you are ↔ top performers used to cling to their posts stay where you are ↔ cling to their posts that's been fundamentally inverted ↔ used to 「过去规则 + 已被反转」直接对应 used to cling（过去常常死守，现在不再）——预 锁定 A。 loyalty of top performers is getting out-dated 把「死守职位」偷换为「忠诚」—— 原文 stay too long 是行为描述（待得太久），不涉及任何 loyalty（忠诚）这一价值评 的）忠诚」。 top performers care more about reputations 中的 reputations 一词出现在第二段 senior managers cautious of letting vague pronouncements cloud their it's safer to stick to the traditional rules 直接复用原文 it's safer to stay where you are 的措辞，但原文紧接着说 that's been fundamentally inverted——传统规则已被`,position:0},{id:30,articleId:"text-2",type:"reading",question:"Which of the following is the best title for the text?",options:{A:"CEOs: Where to Go?",B:"CEOs: All the Way Up?",C:"Top Managers Jump without a Net",D:"The Only Way Out for Top Performers"},answer:"C",analysis:`【判型】Which of the following is the best title for the text 直接要求挑选全文标题，答案必须概 【拆句】Q30 主干是 Which of the following is the best title for the text，which 引导特殊疑问 句，of the following 限定范围；结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。 【选项】A) 答非所问 CEOs: Where to Go? 的核心是「CEO 该去哪里」，但全文没有任何篇幅讨论高管去向 CEOs: All the Way Up?（CEO 们：一路向上？）暗示「裸辞必能上位」的乐观论调， 但第五段 Those who jumped without a job haven't always landed in top positions quickly 与 Marram 等了一年、Willumstad 等了三年的反例已证明：裸辞不总是一路向 C) ✓ 正确 deputy chiefs may be more willing to make the jump without a net ↔ Top Managers Jump without a Net to pursue my goal of running a company ↔ Top Managers Jump without a Net that's been fundamentally inverted ↔ Top Managers Jump without a Net The Only Way Out for Top Performers（顶尖人才的唯一出路）把「裸辞」绝对化为 SENTENCE INSIGHTS · 句子精讲 9 McGee says leaving without a position lined up gave him time to reflect on what kind of company he wanted to run. As boards scrutinize succession plans in response to shareholder pressure, executives who don't get the nod also may wish to move on. In the third quarter, CEO turnover was down 23% from a year ago as nervous boards stuck with the leaders they had, according to Liberum Research. As the economy picks up, opportunities will abound for aspiring leaders. For years executives and headhunters have adhered to the rule that the most attractive CEO candidates are the ones who must be poached. Says Korn/Ferry senior partner Dennis Carey: "I can't think of a single search I've done where a board has not instructed me to look a...`,position:0},{id:31,articleId:"text-3",type:"reading",question:'Consumers may create "earned" media when they are____',options:{A:"obsessed with online shopping at certain Web sites.",B:"inspired by product-promoting e-mails sent to them.",C:"eager to help their friends promote quality products.",D:"enthusiastic about recommending their favorite products."},answer:"D",analysis:'【判型】Consumers may create "earned" media when they are____ 问的是"在什么条件下"，要 【拆句】句子主干是 Consumers may create "earned" media，when 引导时间/条件状语从句、从 句被截断成待补全的 when they are____，四个选项都是该 are 后面的表语，作 they 的状 【定位】P1 Consumers passionate about a product may create "earned" media by willingly promoting it to friends 【选项】A) 无中生有 obsessed with online shopping at certain Web sites 谈的是"对特定网站的网购痴 迷"，原文从未把 earned media 与网购痴迷挂钩。 inspired by product-promoting e-mails sent to them 描述的恰是 a company may leverage "owned" media by sending e-mail alerts about products and sales to customers 这一 owned media 的定义句，与 earned media 的提问对象不符。 eager to help their friends promote quality products 把消费者的动机扭曲为"帮朋友 D) ✓ 正确 passionate about a product ↔ enthusiastic about willingly promoting it to friends ↔ recommending their favorite products 预判的"热情"与"主动推荐"两条锚同时落在 enthusiastic about recommending their favorite products 上，无需推断即可锁定。',position:0},{id:32,articleId:"text-3",type:"reading",question:"According to Paragraph 2, sold media feature____",options:{A:"a safe business environment.",B:"random competition.",C:"strong user traffic.",D:"flexibility in organization."},answer:"C",analysis:'【判型】sold media feature____ 问 sold media 的特征，要求把原文对该术语的定义/属性句客观转 【拆句】According to Paragraph 2, sold media feature____，According to… 为来源状语，主干 sold media feature____ 的 feature 是动词"具有……特征"，四个选项是 feature 的宾语。 【定位】P2 We define such sold media as owned media whose traffic is so strong that other organizations place their content or e-commerce engines within that environment. 【选项】A) 无中生有 a safe business environment 说 sold media 提供"安全的商业环境"，原文从未提及 safe/safety 概念，是凭空添加的属性。 原文 the presence of other marketers makes the site seem objective ... and may help expand user traffic for all companies concerned 强调多方共存是有组织的、互 C) ✓ 正确 owned media whose traffic is so strong that other organizations place their content or e- commerce engines within that environment ↔ strong user traffic flexibility in organization 谈"组织上的灵活性"，原文谈的是流量与互利，从未讨论 sold media 的组织灵活性。',position:0},{id:33,articleId:"text-3",type:"reading",question:"The author indicates in Paragraph 3 that earned media____",options:{A:"invite constant conflicts with passionate consumers.",B:"can be used to produce negative effects in marketing.",C:"may be responsible for fiercer competition.",D:"deserve all the negative comments about them."},answer:"B",analysis:'【判型】The author indicates in Paragraph 3 that earned media____ 中的 indicate 表示"作者暗 【拆句】主干 The author indicates ... that earned media____，in Paragraph 3 是地点状语，that 作者"暗示"的对象是 earned media 而不是 hijacked media。 【定位】P3 Such hijacked media are the opposite of earned media: an asset or campaign becomes hostage to consumers, other stakeholders, or activists who make negative allegations about a brand or product. 【选项】A) 过度推断 invite constant conflicts with passionate consumers 中的 constant 是"持续不断 B) ✓ 正确 Such hijacked media are the opposite of earned media ↔ can be used to produce negative effects in marketing the risk that passionate consumers will voice their opinions in quicker, more visible, and much more damaging ways ↔ negative effects in marketing 在"earned media 在何种意义上具备负面可能"的预判下，四项中只有 can be used to produce negative effects in marketing 与之精确对应。 may be responsible for fiercer competition 把锅扣给"更激烈的竞争"，原文第三段没 deserve all the negative comments about them 说 earned media"应得所有负评"，',position:0},{id:34,articleId:"text-3",type:"reading",question:"Toyota Motor's experience is cited as an example of____",options:{A:"responding effectively to hijacked media.",B:"persuading customers into boycotting products.",C:"cooperating with supportive consumers.",D:"taking advantage of hijacked media."},answer:"A",analysis:`【判型】cited as an example of 明确问"举丰田案例是为了说明什么"，是典型的例证目的题。 【拆句】主干 Toyota Motor's experience is cited as an example of____，is cited as 是被动语 responding effectively to hijacked media 中 responding 是动名词，符合句法）。 【定位】P4 If that happens, passionate consumers would try to persuade others to boycott products, putting the reputation of the target company at risk. In such a case, the company's response may not be sufficiently quick or thoughtful, and the learning curve has been steep. Toyota Motor, for example, alleviated some of the damage from its recall crisis earlier this year with a relatively quick and well-orchestrated social-media response campaign, which included efforts to engage with consumers directly on sites such as Twitter and the social-news site Digg. 【选项】A) ✓ 正确 a relatively quick and well-orchestrated social-media response campaign ↔ responding effectively to hijacked media alleviated some of the damage from its recall crisis ↔ responding effectively Such hijacked media are the opposite of earned media ↔ hijacked media 织、缓解损害"印证有效性；只有 responding effectively to hijacked media 同时覆盖 persuading customers into boycotting products 描述的是 passionate consumers would try to persuade others to boycott products 这一消费者动作，与丰田公司的 cooperating with supportive consumers 中的 supportive consumers（支持的消费 taking advantage of hijacked media 中的 taking advantage of 含"主动利用、获 利"的意味，原文中丰田只是被动"应对、缓解"，并未从 hijacked media 中获益。`,position:0},{id:35,articleId:"text-3",type:"reading",question:"Which of the following is the text mainly about?",options:{A:"Alternatives to conventional paid media.",B:"Conflict between hijacked and earned media.",C:"Dominance of hijacked media.",D:"Popularity of owned media."},answer:"A",analysis:`【判型】Which of the following is the text mainly about? 直接问全文主旨，无任何细节锚。 【拆句】Which of the following is the text mainly about?，主系表结构，主语是 Which of the following，about 后省略了 the text，等同于"下列哪项最能概括本文主题"。结构无陷 阱，关键在 mainly 提示"主线"而非局部。 【选项】A) ✓ 正确 companies today can exploit many alternative forms of media ↔ Alternatives to conventional paid media marketing's impact stems from a broad range of factors beyond conventional paid media ↔ Alternatives to conventional paid media P2 的 owned/sold、P3 的 hijacked、P4 的丰田回应都属于"对传统付费媒体的替代/拓 展"框架，只有 Alternatives to conventional paid media 能把四段统一收拢。 Conflict between hijacked and earned media 只覆盖第三段 Such hijacked media are the opposite of earned media 的局部对比，前后段的 owned/sold/Toyota 案例 Dominance of hijacked media 中的 Dominance（主导/统治）是程度极强的词，原文 Popularity of owned media 只覆盖首段对 owned media 的一笔带过和第二段的 sold media 派生讨论，原文从未论 owned media 的"流行度"，且全文重心远不止 owned。 SENTENCE INSIGHTS · 句子精讲 12 While traditional "paid" media – such as television commercials and print advertisements – still play a major role, companies today can exploit many alternative forms of media. Consumers passionate about a product may create "earned" media by willingly promoting it to friends, and a company may leverage "owned" media by sending e- mail alerts about products and sales to customers registered with its Web site. （passionate about a product、registered with its Web site）和 by 引导的方式状语也是常考结 The way consumers now approach the process of making purchase decisions means that marketing's impac...`,position:0},{id:36,articleId:"text-4",type:"reading",question:"Jennifer Senior suggests in her article that raising a child can bring____",options:{A:"temporary delight.",B:"enjoyment in progress.",C:"happiness in retrospect.",D:"lasting reward."},answer:"C",analysis:'Jennifer Senior 在她的文章中表明，养育孩子可以带来____ 【判型】题干 Jennifer Senior suggests in her article that raising a child can bring 是 someone suggests that 句式，要找的是原文中 Senior 明确说过的话，属客观转述的细节题。 【拆句】Jennifer Senior suggests in her article that raising a child can bring 是一个待补全的不 完整陈述句，主干 Jennifer Senior suggests that raising a child can bring \\_\\_\\_\\_，宾 【定位】P1 Even though the day-to-day experience of raising kids can be soul-crushingly hard, Senior writes that "the very things that in the moment dampen our moods can later be sources of intense gratification and delight." 【选项】A) 与原文相反 temporary delight 的 temporary（短暂的）把养孩子刻画成转瞬即逝的快乐，与定位 enjoyment in progress 暗示养孩子过程中正在进行的享受，与原文 in the moment dampen our moods（当下让人情绪低落）直接冲突。 C) ✓ 正确 can later be sources of intense gratification and delight ↔ happiness in retrospect 预判的「事后回望成喜悦」与 happiness in retrospect 在时间维度（事后）和情感维度 lasting reward 的 lasting（持久的）暗示回报贯穿始终，但原文只说当下煎熬可在事后',position:0},{id:37,articleId:"text-4",type:"reading",question:"We learn from Paragraph 2 that____",options:{A:"celebrity moms are a permanent source for gossip.",B:"single mothers with babies deserve greater attention.",C:"news about pregnant celebrities is entertaining.",D:"having children is highly valued by the public."},answer:"D",analysis:"【判型】We learn from Paragraph 2 that 是「从某段我们可以得知」的客观信息题，答案是该段 【拆句】We learn from Paragraph 2 that 是待补全句，主干 We learn that \\_\\_\\_\\_，结构清晰， 【定位】P2 Practically every week features at least one celebrity mom, or mom-to-be, smiling on the newsstands. 【选项】A) 过度推断 celebrity moms are a permanent source for gossip 的 permanent（永久的） 卦」上。 single mothers with babies deserve greater attention 用 deserve（应得）作主观价 news about pregnant celebrities is entertaining 把段意收缩到「关于怀孕明星的新 D) ✓ 正确 Practically every week features at least one celebrity mom, or mom-to-be, smiling on the newsstands ↔ having children is highly valued by the public highly valued by the public 直接对应。",position:0},{id:38,articleId:"text-4",type:"reading",question:"It is suggested in Paragraph 3 that childless folks____",options:{A:"are constantly exposed to criticism.",B:"are largely ignored by the media.",C:"fail to fulfill their social responsibilities.",D:"are less likely to be satisfied with their life."},answer:"A",analysis:"【判型】It is suggested in Paragraph 3 that childless folks 表面带 suggested 一词，但实指段内 【拆句】It is suggested in Paragraph 3 that childless folks 是 it 形式主语句，真正主语是 that 从 【定位】P3 Unhappy parents rarely are provoked to wonder if they shouldn't have had kids, but unhappy childless folks are bothered with the message that children are the single most important thing in the world: obviously their misery must be a direct result of the gaping baby-size holes in their lives. 【选项】A) ✓ 正确 bothered with the message that children are the single most important thing in the world ↔ are constantly exposed to criticism In a society that so persistently celebrates procreation ↔ are constantly exposed to criticism 预判的「持续承受舆论压力」在 are constantly exposed to criticism 中同时落到 constantly（持续）和 criticism（批评/压力）两个核心成分上。 are largely ignored by the media 说无子女者基本被媒体忽略，但原文 bothered fail to fulfill their social responsibilities 说无子女者未尽社会责任，但原文只描述他们 来质疑这种舆论对他们 doesn't seem quite fair）。 are less likely to be satisfied with their life 直接断言无子女者更不容易对生活满意，",position:0},{id:39,articleId:"text-4",type:"reading",question:"According to Paragraph 4, the message conveyed by celebrity magazines is____",options:{A:"soothing.",B:"ambiguous.",C:"compensatory.",D:"misleading."},answer:"D",analysis:'A) 抚慰人心的。 B) 模糊不清的。 C) 补偿性的。 D) 误导性的。 【判型】According to Paragraph 4, the message conveyed by celebrity magazines is 问的是 【拆句】According to Paragraph 4, the message conveyed by celebrity magazines is 是待补全 句，主干 the message is \\_\\_\\_\\_，conveyed by celebrity magazines 是过去分词作后置 【定位】P4 Of course, the image of parenthood that celebrity magazines like Us Weekly and People present is hugely unrealistic, especially when the parents are single mothers like Bullock. 【选项】A) 与原文相反 明确的（hugely unrealistic），并非含糊。 D) ✓ 正确 hugely unrealistic ↔ misleading yet to hear Sandra and Britney tell it, raising a kid on their "own" (read: with round-the-clock help) is a piece of cake ↔ misleading 预判的「失实」与 misleading 在内容真实性（unrealistic）与读者效果（误导）两层上',position:0},{id:40,articleId:"text-4",type:"reading",question:`Which of the following can be inferred from the last paragraph? Part B Directions: The following paragraphs are given in a wrong order. For questions 41 -45, you are required to reorganize these paragraphs into a coherent text by choosing from the list A-G and filling them into the numbered boxes. Paragraphs E and G have been correctly placed. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points) Menand points out, become a lawyer in three years and a medical doctor in four. But the regular time it takes to get a doctoral degree in the humanities is nine years. Not surprisingly, up to half of all doctoral students in English drop out before getting their degrees. disciplines that are going out of style: 22% of American college graduates now major in business compared with only 2% in history and 4% in English. However, many leading American universities want their undergraduates to have a grounding in the basic canon of ideas that every educated person should possess. But most find it difficult to agree on what a "general education" should look like. At Harvard, Mr. Menand notes, "the great books are read because they have been read" – they form a sort of social glue. There are simply too few posts. This is partly because universities continue to produce ever more PhDs. But fewer students want to study humanities subjects: English departments awarded more bachelor's degrees in 1970-71 than they did 20 years later. Fewer students require fewer teachers. So, at the end of a decade of thesis-writing, many humanities students leave the profession to do something for which they have not been trained. American universities that liberal-arts education and professional education should be kept separate, taught in different schools. Many students experience both varieties. Although more than half of Harvard undergraduates end up in law, medicine or business, future doctors and lawyers must study a non-specialist liberal-arts degree before embarking on a professional qualification. [ E ] Besides professionalising the professions by this separation, top American universities have professionalised the professor. The growth in public money for academic research has speeded the process: federal research grants rose fourfold between 1960 and 1990, but faculty teaching hours fell by half as research took its toll. Professionalism has turned the acquisition of a doctoral degree into a prerequisite for a successful academic career: as late as 1969 a third of American professors did not possess one. But the key idea behind professionalisation, argues Mr. Menand, is that "the knowledge and skills needed for a particular specialisation are transmissible but not transferable." So disciplines acquire a monopoly not just over the production of knowledge, but also over the production of the producers of knowledge. [ F ] The key to reforming higher education, concludes Mr. Menand, is to alter the way in which "the producers of knowledge are produced". Otherwise, academics will continue to think dangerously alike, increasingly detached from the societies which they study, investigate and criticise. "Academic inquiry, at least in some fields, may need to become less exclusionary and more holistic." Yet quite how that happens, Mr. Menand does not say. [ G ] The subtle and intelligent little book The Marketplace of Ideas: Reform and Resistance in the American University should be read by every student thinking of applying to take a doctoral degree. They may then decide to go elsewhere. For something curious has been happening in American universities, and Louis Menand, a professor of English at Harvard University, captured it skillfully. G → 41. → 42. → E → 43. → 44. → 45. Part C Directions: Read the following text carefully and then translate the underlined segments into Chinese. Write your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. ( 10 points) With its theme that "Mind is the master weaver," creating our inner character and outer circumstances, the book As a Man Thinketh by James Allen is an in-depth exploration of the central idea of self-help writing. (46)Allen's contribution was to take an assumption we all share – that because we are not robots we therefore control our thoughts – and reveal its erroneous nature. Because most of us believe that mind is separate from matter, we think that thoughts can be hidden and made powerless; this allows us to think one way and act another. However, Allen believed that the unconscious mind generates as much action as the conscious mind, and (47)while we may be able to sustain the illusion of control through the conscious mind alone, in reality we are continually faced with a question: "Why cannot I make myself do this or achieve that?" Since desire and will are damaged by the presence of thoughts that do not accord with desire, Allen concluded: "We do not attract what we want, but what we are." Achievement happens because you as a person embody the external achievement; you don't "get" success but become it. There is no gap between mind and matter. Part of the fame of Allen's book is its contention that "Circumstances do not make a person, they reveal him." (48)This seems a justification for neglect of those in need, and a rationalization of exploitation, of the superiority of those at the top and the inferiority of those at the bottom. This, however, would be a knee-jerk reaction to a subtle argument. Each set of circumstances, however bad, offers a unique opportunity for growth. If circumstances always determined the life and prospects of people, then humanity would never have progressed. In fact, (49)circumstances seem to be designed to bring out the best in us, and if we feel that we have been "wronged" then we are unlikely to begin a conscious effort to escape from our situation. Nevertheless, as any biographer knows, a person's early life and its conditions are often the greatest gift to an individual. The sobering aspect of Allen's book is that we have no one else to blame for our present condition except ourselves. (50)The upside is the possibilities contained in knowing that everything is up to us; where before we were experts in the array of limitations, now we become authorities of what is possible.`,options:{A:"No disciplines have seized on professionalism with as much enthusiasm as the humanities. You can, Mr.",B:"His concern is mainly with the humanities: literature, languages, philosophy and so on. These are",C:"Equally unsurprisingly, only about half end up with professorships for which they entered graduate school.",D:"One reason why it is hard to design and teach such courses is that they cut across the insistence by top"},answer:"B",analysis:`【判型】Which of the following can be inferred from the last paragraph 明含 inferred，要求 【拆句】Which of the following can be inferred from the last paragraph 是疑问句，主干 Which can be inferred from the last paragraph？结构平铺，无陷阱。 【定位】P5 But it's interesting to wonder if the images we see every week of stress-free, happiness- enhancing parenthood aren't in some small, subconscious way contributing to our own dissatisfactions with the actual experience, in the same way that a small part of us hoped getting "the Rachel" might make us look just a little bit like Jennifer Aniston. 有一小部分人盼着剪个「The Rachel」发型就能让自己看起来有点像 Jennifer Aniston。 【选项】A) 答非所问 Having children contributes little to the glamour of celebrity moms 讨论的是「生 B) ✓ 正确 the images we see every week of stress-free, happiness-enhancing parenthood aren't in some small, subconscious way contributing to our own dissatisfactions with the actual experience ↔ Celebrity moms have influenced our attitude towards child rearing in some small, subconscious way ↔ Celebrity moms have influenced our attitude towards child rearing Celebrity moms have influenced our attitude towards child rearing 在两层上都恰 Having children intensifies our dissatisfaction with life 说「生孩子加剧了我们对生 活的不满」，把原文 our own dissatisfactions with the actual experience 中的 the actual experience（指育儿这一具体体验）偷换成 life（整个生活），且把「明星形象 We sometimes neglect the happiness from child rearing 说「我们有时忽视了育儿 SENTENCE INSIGHTS · 句子精讲 6 Even though the day-to-day experience of raising kids can be soul-crushingly ...`,position:0}]}],s={id:e,year:2011,subject:t,title:a,sections:i};export{s as default,e as id,i as sections,t as subject,a as title,o as year};
